#  RW-WPS authored authority for ECMWF open-data GRIB2 (IFS oper and AIFS
#  single, 0.25-degree lat-lon).  Authored from real 2026-08-16/17 00Z bytes
#  through grib2_inventory: the soil column rides generalized surface 151 by
#  ordinal pair (sot 2-3-18, vsw 2-0-25) carried in the Level1/Level2
#  columns, 2 m humidity is published as dewpoint (the ecmwf map-source rule
#  derives RH), and terrain is the surface geopotential (SOILGEO -> SOILHGT
#  rule).  GRIB1 columns carry the t128 analogues so the parser admits the
#  rows; this table is authored for the GRIB2 products.  AIFS matches a
#  subset: no pressure-level RH (use --use-spechumd yes) and two soil
#  ordinals.
# Snow: ECMWF centre 98, local table 1, GRIB2 0-1-254 is sd in metres of
# water equivalent. The existing SNOW_EC rule multiplies by 1000. The blank
# SNOW selector is an output declaration, not another decoded field.
# Sea ice: 10-2-0 is an area fraction. A thickness field (10-2-1) is never
# selected as fraction. When the primary omits fraction, a same-valid-time
# fraction-only donor can be an additional input to the same writer.
# SOILGEO is scratch. The blank SOILHGT selector declares the derived
# SOILGEO / 9.81 output. Without that declaration the writer computes the
# height but drops it, leaving the init's source terrain at zero.
#  AIFS ENS (aifs-ens row): the open-data AIFS ENS members publish pressure-level
#  geopotential z (0-3-4 on level 100) and no gh, so the row above selects it as
#  GEOPT and the writer derives HGT = GEOPT / 9.81 (met_intermediate hgt_from_geopt).
#  Measured on the 2026-10-23 12Z enfo-cf/pf indexes, 2026-10-24.
